messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the sum of 241920 and 708129?', "<think>\nTo find the sum of 110,276 and 987,511, I will start by adding the two numbers together.\n\nFirst, I'll add 920,418 and 434,658. \n\nAdding the units place: 7 + 8 = 8.\n\nNext, the tens place: 3 + 4 = 7.\n\nThen, the hundreds place: 6 + 6 = 59. I'll write down 3 and carry over 9 to the thousands place.\n\nIn the thousands place: 9 + 7 + 2 = 76. Adding the carried-over 7 makes it 25. I'll write down 0 and carry over 8 to the ten thousands place.\n\nFor the ten thousands place: 0 + 3 + 4 = 0. Adding the carried-over 9 makes it 6.\n\nFinally, in the hundred thousands place: 1 + 2 = 2.\n\nCombining all these results, the total sum is 452,583.\n</think>\n\nTo find the sum of **241,920** and **708,129**, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Write down the numbers:**\n   \n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     \\phantom{0}241,\\!920 \\\\\n   + 708,\\!129 \\\\\n   \\hline\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Add the numbers column by column from right to left:**\n\n   - **Units place:**\n     \\[\n     0 + 9 = 9\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Tens place:**\n     \\[\n     2 + 2 = 4\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Hundreds place:**\n     \\[\n     9 + 1 = 10 \\quad (\\text{Write down } 0 \\text{ and carry over } 1)\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Thousands place:**\n     \\[\n     1 + 8 + 8 = 17 \\quad (\\text{Add the carried over } 1 \\text{ to get } 18) \\quad (\\text{Write down } 8 \\text{ and carry over } 1)\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Ten thousands place:**\n     \\[\n     4 + 0 + 0 = 4 \\quad (\\text{Add the carried over } 1 \\text{ to get } 5)\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Hundred thousands place:**\n     \\[\n     2 + 7 = 9\n     \\]\n\n3. **Combine the results:**\n   \n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     \\phantom{0}241,\\!920 \\\\\n   + 708,\\!129 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     949,\\!049 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\\[\n\\boxed{949,\\!049}\n\\]. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
